@@name
add-feature
@@description
Implement the functionality described in the user request, integrated the way the surrounding code already does similar things.
@@requirements
    - Find the closest existing feature and follow its structure, naming and error handling
    - Cover the new behaviour with tests, including at least one edge or failure case
    - Update user-facing documentation or help text if the feature is visible to users
@@approach
    Before implementing, reason through:
    - Which existing module owns this responsibility, and what its public interface is
    - Inputs, defaults and failure modes of the new behaviour
    Select a design that fits the existing patterns and commit to it.
@@verification
    - Exercise the new behaviour end to end (command, request or test) and confirm the expected result
@@constraints
    - Existing behaviour and public interfaces stay backward compatible unless the request says otherwise
    - No placeholder implementations, TODO stubs or hard-coded sample data
@@out-of-scope
    - Features or options the request does not ask for
